From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t20: forward private ioctls from the video-in to the core

The vendor libimp sends the frame-source private commands
(TX_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL_FRAME_CHAN_*) to the video-in device.  The
video-in subdev only handled the standard input, sensor-register and
stream ioctls; VIDIOC_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL fell through the default case,
so IMP_FrameSource_EnableChn() failed with -1 before any frame-channel
buffer was queued.

Forward the private ioctl to the ISP core subdev, which already
implements the FRAME_CHAN_* commands.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-video-in.c
+++ b/driver/t20/sdk/source/tx-isp-video-in.c
@@ -520,6 +520,18 @@
 		case VIDIOC_STREAMOFF:
 			ret = subdev_core_ops_streamoff(vi, 0);
 			break;
+		case VIDIOC_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL:
+			/*
+			 * The vendor libimp sends the frame-source commands
+			 * (TX_ISP_PRIVATE_IOCTL_FRAME_CHAN_*) to this device.
+			 * They are implemented by the ISP core, not by the
+			 * video-in subdev, so pass them through.
+			 */
+			if (vi->p && vi->p->subdevs[TX_ISP_CORE_GRP_IDX])
+				ret = v4l2_subdev_call(
+					vi->p->subdevs[TX_ISP_CORE_GRP_IDX],
+					core, ioctl, cmd, arg);
+			break;
 		default:
 			break;
 	}
